{"contract":"rgp-pems2-admission-transaction/2","expected_base_sha256":"9d9a20b664c3b8f352abe0ea085a1de97823b749da9f8b73ca6df812e9cb482a","new_records":[{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The operator-management contract permits authority-grant-derived approval only for exact non-root `operator-registry.disable` proposals; protected-root transfer remains explicitly non-delegable."},"id":"pems:proposition:198c6296d79a8c129d34b28e","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:f139b9988c81888789c4c2b0"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The operator-registry contract makes operator events authoritative and the current operator file a deterministic projection, and initial-root establishment creates administrative operator identity without granting semantic-reconciliation or admission authority."},"id":"pems:proposition:22340433f0da64466247b028","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:d2d6340e7d900a49e8b16b37"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The distillation-ingestion operation constructs an invocation request and activation bundle without calling a model or mutating canonical knowledge, and excludes `.git/`, `.reasoning-distiller/`, and `project-knowledge/` from evidence selection."},"id":"pems:proposition:23e1493f255d1a1845c2e89a","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:b93a939fcd815c32eef97dcc"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Steward-authorization contract defines `semantic_reconciliation` and `admission` as independent scopes, makes authorization events authoritative with a derived current projection, and states that registration alone never grants a Steward scope."},"id":"pems:proposition:2b44034c925803193972b8a2","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:375f41d690b6aa1a302a6086"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The common mutation substrate preserves a distinction between direct-operator approval and authority-grant-derived approval while binding both approval forms to exactly one immutable proposal."},"id":"pems:proposition:34d6c6215b81f193adb86866","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:92e7d90af82bbbb3fee32005"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The role-registry contract states that registry membership grants no Steward, reconciliation, admission, protocol-governance, or invocation authority and that the package-provided `steward:default` role is immutable, always available, and never authorized merely by registration."},"id":"pems:proposition:3e64180ab1b48d90c47559c3","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:0c4ca9d8a93b77175926461f"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The exceptional-recovery contract requires the protected root, preserves damaged authoritative history byte-for-byte, binds approval to the exact damaged-history fingerprint and continuation state, and stores recovery separately as append-only evidence."},"id":"pems:proposition:4803336f933dbbba4402757c","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:f72f749511140a2f2f6f189a"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The RIL activation-evidence contract validates one exact runtime invocation, registered role, requested Steward scope, current role availability, and current Steward assignment; authorization or role-name matching alone is insufficient."},"id":"pems:proposition:485534addefcb9c5085f1735","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:6a73af3164f2a564a3c23f62"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The storage-verification contract defines R14 as a read-only check of canonical PEMS schema/integrity, deterministic PEMS bytes, exact COVE encoding and round-trip, and a matching immutable admission receipt."},"id":"pems:proposition:4b6f97b6dbe398af6eeb1be0","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:7b624fdc6b0ba84ff632352e"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The governed-ingestion operation requires governed evidence to be explicitly selected and states that source authority must not be inferred from filenames, directories, headings, source identifiers, or prose."},"id":"pems:proposition:5e53cea62207805bc1f55a90","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:f03196d665d7e7ddd1f2519b"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The project-identity amendment requires first admission to construct a project-seeded PEMS/2 base from valid project/2 identity and requires admission to fail with PROJECT_IDENTITY_REQUIRED when neither valid v2 project identity nor existing canonical PEMS is available."},"id":"pems:proposition:61e05ab20e4667baaa5fb2a1","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:ca3e586db98ce8ffdf89c957"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The RIL activation-evidence primitive is read-only, persists no activation state, grants no authority, and requires downstream authority-bearing primitives to receive or bind the exact activation artifact or digest they validated."},"id":"pems:proposition:706fbb6e0d5a2305dc242236","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:6a73af3164f2a564a3c23f62"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The common mutation substrate defines proposals as immutable intent with no mutation, approvals as exact-proposal-bound authority evidence, append-only mutation events as authoritative state, and projections as derived replay products."},"id":"pems:proposition:7d633e56b3fabb2e36c43dfc","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:92e7d90af82bbbb3fee32005"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The orchestrator-composition contract makes R15 composition-only: it must delegate to existing primitives, must not synthesize authority-sensitive inputs, and must preserve delegated primitive results without reinterpretation."},"id":"pems:proposition:7d8d8bc0035fc0f06910d9c0","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:fb55f550f55667fb0a6c415c"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The production invocation contract fixes the evidence set before model activation and prohibits the Distiller from autonomously searching for additional project facts or inferring authority from source identifiers or locators."},"id":"pems:proposition:81c2bf7c2261bad97b00e2e7","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:7274f7c8af5bbd1a362e4f59"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The project-identity amendment retains exact v1 bootstrap configuration as a compatibility state and permits v1-to-v2 migration only when all v2 identity fields are explicitly supplied."},"id":"pems:proposition:85d79e6e23ff68cdada3e885","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:ca3e586db98ce8ffdf89c957"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The common mutation substrate requires grant applicability, scope, availability, consumption accounting, approval creation, and the grant approval-issued event to be atomic with respect to grant normative state; stale races fail rather than rebase."},"id":"pems:proposition:8669c44871afa130b400b86b","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:92e7d90af82bbbb3fee32005"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The ordinary-repair contract permits deterministic replacement or recreation of derived projections only after authoritative replay succeeds; invalid event history stops with exceptional-recovery-required and no mutation."},"id":"pems:proposition:8d280d53fa484e2d57839a08","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:d10a2299a8b934c905acecfb"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Steward-authorization contract requires an authorized human operator to approve an exact Steward-scope proposal and states that the approving operator does not thereby become a Steward."},"id":"pems:proposition:8dde72ffd3f4d5823a5c8d5b","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:375f41d690b6aa1a302a6086"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The project-identity amendment defines `reasoning-distiller-project/2` with explicit project-owned id, name, repository, and summary fields and prohibits the framework from inferring those identity fields from repository or environment state."},"id":"pems:proposition:9b7d13b1071a08fc98462842","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:ca3e586db98ce8ffdf89c957"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The project bootstrap contract defines bootstrap as a deterministic creator of minimum project-owned invocation/evidence/submission structure and explicitly excludes operator, Steward, canonical, admission, evidence-fact, and role authority creation."},"id":"pems:proposition:9d1555e3ad1c44767c0eb9f5","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:b5608823c9d1b4b545275383"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The production invocation contract makes request validation, evidence digest checks, activation-bundle construction, RGP validation, submission identity, persistence rules, and failure classification deterministic for fixed local inputs."},"id":"pems:proposition:a5fb6ec8cdf893823853352e","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:7274f7c8af5bbd1a362e4f59"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The composite-status contract defines status as a read-only projection over independently reportable lifecycle dimensions, applies explicit blocker precedence, and distinguishes REBUILDABLE projection state from corruption without repairing it."},"id":"pems:proposition:abe528b2013354401c957e8c","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:9fcc34692a5937871b408f14"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The operator-management contract prohibits ordinary operator mutations from disabling, demoting, removing, or otherwise mutating the protected root and defines root transfer as a separate current-root-approved ceremony."},"id":"pems:proposition:b18c7da7e9ca662b1e6cdb0a","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:f139b9988c81888789c4c2b0"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The production invocation contract grants the Distiller neither semantic-reconciliation nor admission authority and restricts its semantic project writes to the configured raw candidate artifact and valid candidate submission."},"id":"pems:proposition:b323fc3103599b32373489c3","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:7274f7c8af5bbd1a362e4f59"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The production invocation contract requires raw candidate bytes to be preserved unchanged and prohibits post-model semantic repair, normalization, proposition insertion, kind changes, or provenance rewriting."},"id":"pems:proposition:b8474873fa869037f8a0438e","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:7274f7c8af5bbd1a362e4f59"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The operator-registry contract states that installation and bootstrap create no operator authority and requires an explicit initial-root ceremony before the first authority-sensitive operation when no operator registry exists."},"id":"pems:proposition:c59d6ac34ff4998565da9209","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:d2d6340e7d900a49e8b16b37"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The admission contract requires immutable activation, plan, and receipt evidence and permits exact retry as NO_CHANGE only when the receipt and canonical PEMS/COVE bytes agree with the originally admitted result."},"id":"pems:proposition:c96f7d259014776d56cc50f6","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:811a953e5f0e154109c7a8a3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The common mutation substrate requires independent apply-time proposal, basis, state, and governing-domain validation for every authority basis and does not require a previously valid grant-derived approval to lose validity merely because its grant was later revoked."},"id":"pems:proposition:cfa556497cf1149d8d66bb20","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:92e7d90af82bbbb3fee32005"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The reconciliation contract writes one immutable candidate-bound disposition from an explicit assessment only after activation validates for `semantic_reconciliation`, and prohibits reconciliation from invoking admission or mutating canonical PEMS/COVE stores."},"id":"pems:proposition:d47a1b5e7c1756bd29b5b80d","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:3a052db1a1295ccf9b4b606c"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The current production-invocation status record reports PASS and records both canonical-mutation authority and semantic-reconciliation authority as false."},"id":"pems:proposition:e8c06a0aeec27e34bc976e75","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:343890a90be4e73cd3c3938f"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The role-registry contract rejects consumer `rd:*` capabilities and consumer-side Architect or RGP Engineer protocol-governance roles, and requires snapshot submissions to declare explicit role-id scope so absence only affects roles inside that scope."},"id":"pems:proposition:ed2fef80c77cc9cc742c197e","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:0c4ca9d8a93b77175926461f"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The admission contract makes R13 the only RIL primitive in its slice allowed to mutate canonical PEMS/COVE and requires a compatible recommended disposition, exact candidate identity, independent admission-scope activation, an exact transaction plan, current-base hash match, and deterministic COVE round-trip."},"id":"pems:proposition:f447db4932dafe4b1ebaa3ff","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:811a953e5f0e154109c7a8a3"]}},{"data":{"authority":"repository_state","identity_locator":{"path":"docs/operations/RIL_OPERATOR_MANAGEMENT_CONTRACT.md","repository":"loteque/reasoning-distiller"},"source_kind":"repository_file"},"id":"pems:source:10f727a5913ba646327e4ace","kind":"source","lifecycle":"current"},{"data":{"authority":"repository_state","identity_locator":{"path":"docs/operations/PROJECT_IDENTITY_FIRST_ADMISSION_AMENDMENT.md","repository":"loteque/reasoning-distiller"},"source_kind":"repository_file"},"id":"pems:source:1ef1c09ed820abbaaf4bf5c5","kind":"source","lifecycle":"current"},{"data":{"authority":"repository_state","identity_locator":{"path":"docs/operations/DISTILLATION_INGESTION.md","repository":"loteque/reasoning-distiller"},"source_kind":"repository_file"},"id":"pems:source:1fa9083877b34229e1f89c42","kind":"source","lifecycle":"current"},{"data":{"authority":"repository_state","identity_locator":{"path":"docs/operations/RIL_ORDINARY_REPAIR_CONTRACT.md","repository":"loteque/reasoning-distiller"},"source_kind":"repository_file"},"id":"pems:source:26e972cfa3cbb53ffbe561ae","kind":"source","lifecycle":"current"},{"data":{"authority":"repository_state","identity_locator":{"path":"docs/operations/PRODUCTION_INVOCATION_CONTRACT.md","repository":"loteque/reasoning-distiller"},"source_kind":"repository_file"},"id":"pems:source:36810a3acebed655a70bf2f5","kind":"source","lifecycle":"current"},{"data":{"authority":"repository_state","identity_locator":{"path":"docs/operations/RIL_COMMON_MUTATION_CONTRACT.md","repository":"loteque/reasoning-distiller"},"source_kind":"repository_file"},"id":"pems:source:5fe3fca70fd64a57655bfeee","kind":"source","lifecycle":"current"},{"data":{"authority":"reposito